.TH LUSTRE.ENABLE_FLR_EC 4 2026-08-12 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lustre.enable_flr_ec \- request erasure coded FLR layout support on a client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.B lctl get_param --module lustre.enable_flr_ec
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param --module lustre.enable_flr_ec=" 0 | 1
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-client node, for all filesystems mounted afterwards.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB enable_flr_ec= 0
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB enable_flr_ec= 0
.br
.RB enable_flr_ec= 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
Whether this client asks the MDS for erasure coded FLR layout support
when it mounts a filesystem.
When set, the client tells the MDS that it understands the
.B parity
layout pattern.  An MDS from 2.18.0 on replies with the pattern types both
ends support, see
.BR mdt.layout_pattern_types (4);
an older MDS cannot filter the list and the client keeps what it asked for.
The result is visible as
.BR lov.layout_pattern_types (4).
.PP
When it is not set the client requests only the pre-2.18 baseline of
.BR raid0 ", " mdt " and " overstriped ,
and treats components with any other pattern as unusable: reading such a
file works only if it has another mirror.
Such a client still writes to the data mirror of an erasure coded file, and
those writes mark the overlapping parity components stale so that a later
.BR lfs-mirror-resync (1)
from a capable client rebuilds them, but resyncing an erasure coded mirror
from the client itself fails.
Creating erasure coded files also needs
.B llite.*.enable_erasure_coding
to be set.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B lustre.enable_flr_ec
.EE
It is a parameter of the
.B lustre
client module, so
.B lctl
needs
.B --module
to reach it.
It can also be set at module load time with an
.B "options lustre enable_flr_ec=1"
line in a
.BR modprobe.d (5)
configuration file.
.PP
The
.B mdt
module has a separate
.B mdt_enable_flr_ec
parameter that sets the MDT side default.
.SH CAVEATS
The value is read when a filesystem is mounted, so a change only affects
subsequent mounts.  A filesystem that is already mounted keeps requesting
the layout types it asked for at mount time until it is remounted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Request EC layout support for filesystems mounted from now on:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param --module lustre.enable_flr_ec=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B enable_flr_ec
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_60
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-mirror-create (1),
.BR lov.layout_pattern_types (4),
.BR mdt.layout_pattern_types (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
